SUMMARY:Barbecue and Hike through Tommy Thompson Park.
DESCRIPTION:These Boots Are Made for Hiking\nLocation: Meet at the entranc
 e of Tommy Thompson Park -Leslie Street Spit\n**It's time to have some fun
 !**\nWhat better way to celebrate the end of Summer with a barbecue by the
  lake. Join us for burgers and drinks **under the tents** and on the water
  at Ashbridges Bay for burgers and drinks!\n($10. For a burger and drink.)
 \n\nPlease etransfer $10 to boots4hikingthesix@gmail.com and add your pref
 erence for meat or veggie burger in the comment. Etransfers are required b
 y Wednesday\, Sept 23rd\n\nAfter a 8km hike (with some fun things happenin
 g along the way) at Tommy Thompson Park we will head to Ashbridges Bay for
  burgers- veggie and meat.\nFeel free to bring alcoholic beverages\, and b
 oard games - We will have a beach ball.\n\nTommy Thompson Park is a man-ma
 de urban wilderness and wildlife sanctuary built on the Leslie Street Spit
 \, stretching 5 kilometers to Lake Ontario.\nManaged by the Toronto and Re
 gion Conservation Authority\, this unique park offers a peaceful escape fr
 om the city with a mix of wetlands\, meadows\, and trails.\nA unique place
  near downtown Toronto to experience nature\, and *one of the best places 
 for bird-watching in the city*\, with more than 300 recorded species!
