X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Youth Hub: Orange Shirt Day Beaded Pin Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T170000
UID:6aadac09607483003827f535@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Orange Shirt Day and National Day for Truth and Reconciliation
  are observed annually on September 30. In this workshop\, Brianna Patrick
 \, Objiway beading artist\, will explain the significance of Orange Shirt 
 Day and guide participants in the creation of individual Orange Shirt Day 
 pins that raise awareness and recognize the historical and ongoing trauma 
 that Indigenous peoples experience as a result of the residential school s
 ystem. Presenter will be virtual\, but program is in person.\nAll teens ar
 e welcome! Drop-in\, no registration required.\nThis program is part of Yo
 uth Hub service. Youth Hubs are a welcoming place for teens after school a
 nd in the summer\, where helpful staff are always available. Free\, nutri
 tious snacks are offered daily. Drop by a branch with a\nYouth Hub\nor ca
 ll the branch to find out more.
LOCATION:Northern District\, Youth Hub (on the second floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aadac09607483003827f535
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
