X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b47e69166f088b933f31"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Fat Fables: Resisting Fatphobia and Finding Fat Joy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T200000
UID:6a85b47e69166f088b933f31@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join artists\, Jules Vodarek Hunter and Morgan Davis\, co-crea
 tors of\nFat Fables\n\, for an evening of learning\, performance and makin
 g connections.\nFat Fables\nis a performance and creation program for Fat 
 Two-Spirit\, Lesbian\, Gay\, Bisexual\, Trans\, Queer\, Intersex\, Asexual
  (2SLGBTQIA+) folks. The facilitators will share its positive impact in ce
 lebrating and uplifting different bodies\, discuss the origins of fatphobi
 a and how it shapes the current state of affairs on all bodies today.\nPho
 to Credit: Jae Yang\nA brief excerpt from the book\, Belly of the Beast: t
 he Politics of Anti-fatness as Anti-blackness by Da'Shaun Harrison\, will 
 be read to spark an open conversation. With size-inclusive seating and co
 zy welcoming vibes\, the facilitators will lead a creative writing session
 \, where attendees can write\, share\, and participate as much or as littl
 e as they want.\nThe goal of Fat Fables is to create community for fat que
 er and trans folks\, to tell stories\, and to dream of a fat future where 
 we all thrive. Fat people deserve to be visible\, to be seen and to be art
 ists on stage.\nThe program aims to help attendees feel empowered\, suppor
 ted\, and to leave with a full heart.\nRegistration required.\nFree. Doors
  open for registrants at 5:45 pm. At 6:00 pm\, spots become first-come\, f
 irst-served until capacity is reached. The program will run from 6 pm to 8
  pm.\nThis program is produced by\nOntario Culture Days\nin collaboration 
 with\nSummerWorks\nas Producing Partner and Toronto Public Library. This p
 rogram is supported by the City of Toronto.\nOntario Culture Days is a pro
 vince-wide festival made possible through the support of its foundational 
 partners\, the Province of Ontario and the Ontario Arts Council. We acknow
 ledge the support of the Canada Council for the Arts and the Government of
  Canada.
LOCATION:Parkdale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a85b47e69166f088b933f31
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
