UID:6a6d6713e9de6536001fb0e6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn how to edit and enhance photos using Pixlr\, a free onli
 ne photo editor. Participants will explore tools such as Zoom\, Pan\, Crop
 \, Clone\, and Heal\, and learn basic photo adjustments including brightne
 ss\, contrast\, hue\, saturation\, and levels. Participants will take home
  a mini photo frame with a printed photo of their choice.  Keyboarding and
  mouse skills are required. .\nKeyboarding and mouse skills are required.\
 nRegistration is required.\nRegistration begins on August 28th at 9 a.m.\
 nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes of the start of th
 e program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on th
 is form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librar
 ies Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be
