BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84d430be148200298841f5"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_teens
SUMMARY:Percussion Basics with LMMS
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T200000
UID:6a84d430be148200298841f5@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Odd-time beatmaking and sampling basics using Linux MultiMedia
  Studio & Audacity.\nLinux MultiMedia Studio is a digital audio workstatio
 n\, or DAW. It is a sound generation system\, synthesizer\, beat/bassline 
 editor and MIDI control system that can power a small home music studio. S
 ounds\, tones and rhythms can be generated\, played\, and artfully arrange
 d to create entire tracks. Tracks can then be layered to create songs\, wh
 ich can later be saved to an output format.\nThis percussion workshop is d
 ivided into two separate sections:\nOdd-time beatmaking\nSampling basics u
 sing Linux MultiMedia Studio + Audacity\nAn odd\, irregular or unequal sub
 division of a beat can be difficult to play but do have patterns that are 
 discernable for the performer. The most common irregular metres mix simple
  time (whose basic note division is in groups of two)\, and compound time 
 (threes) together within a single measure. Odd-time polyrhythms commonly a
 ppear in Latin\, West African and other musical genres.\nA sample is the u
 se of a portion of an existing song\, recontextualized for a substantially
  new recording such as a drumbeat. The point is to make a new original tra
 ck using a sample from a previous song. Sampling has its historical roots 
 in tape-looping\, turntablism (DJing) and drum machines\, and can be heard
  in avant-garde\, Hip Hop and other genres.\nKeyboarding and mouse skills 
 are required.\nRegistration is required.\nRegistration begins on September
  14th at 12:30pm.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed after 5 minutes 
 of the start of the program.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal
  information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under
  the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The inform
 ation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and 
 evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can b
 e directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 78
 9 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor - eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84d430be148200298841f5
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a38455390cc4e3a790fb58c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260928T193000
UID:6a38455390cc4e3a790fb58c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Emergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In Canada\, we fa
 ce numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heatwaves\, and ear
 thquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual and household eme
 rgency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by the\nToronto Em
 ergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in partnership with
  the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:\nThe potential
  hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergency plan\nHow to 
 assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and support networks d
 uring emergencies\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal informatio
 n on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public
  Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will 
 only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation.
  Questions about how the library handles your information can be directed 
 to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Str
 eet\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Palmerston\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a38455390cc4e3a790fb58c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
