X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/315674369/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_microsoft_reactor_toronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_315674369@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045639Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T130000
SUMMARY:Composing Knowledge Bases That Reason Over Work\, Business\, and t
 he Web
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nLearn how to design knowledge bases
  that span multiple domains. This session focuses on retrieval strategies 
 that bring together work data\, structured business context\, and real-tim
 e web signals.\n\nWe’ll explore how to orchestrate these sources so agen
 ts can reason across them effectively\, rather than treating each in isola
 tion.\n\n***\n\n🔗 Resources: https://aka.ms/iq-series\n\n📌 This even
 t is a part of a series\, learn more here: https://aka.ms/microsoftiqlive\
 n\n#MSFTReactor #learnconnectbuild #foundryiq #serverless #knowledgebases 
 #agentdevelopment #retrieval #datagrounding #azureaifoundry #enterprisekno
 wledge
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3156
 74369/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260713T234142Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260713T234142Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Microsoft Reactor Toronto": "https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/316613810/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_microsoft_reactor_toronto
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Microsoft Reactor Toronto
UID:event_316613810@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045639Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T133000
SUMMARY:Let's Learn GitHub Copilot SDK (.NET)
DESCRIPTION:Microsoft Reactor Toronto\nJoin this beginner-friendly livestr
 eam to learn how to build agentic applications with the GitHub Copilot SDK
  for .NET\, without implementing the agent loop yourself. Unlike calling a
  model API directly\, the SDK gives your application programmatic access t
 o Copilot’s agent runtime\, including conversation management\, planning
 \, tool orchestration\, streaming events\, and session state. During the s
 ession\, we’ll explore clients\, sessions\, prompts\, and the agent runt
 ime. You’ll learn how to create multi-turn conversations\, stream respon
 ses in real time\, expose application functions as tools\, connect externa
 l capabilities through MCP servers\, and control agent behavior with hooks
  and permission handlers. We’ll also help you understand when to use the
  Copilot SDK instead of the interactive Copilot CLI: use the CLI for devel
 oper tasks in the terminal\, and use the SDK when you want to embed Copilo
 t’s agentic capabilities in your own application or service. No prior ex
 perience with the GitHub Copilot SDK is required.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/microsoft-reactor-toronto/events/3166
 13810/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260918T172049Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T172049Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
