SUMMARY:Build & Brand Your Online Shop: WordPress for Small Business
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:6a8868b44cb69d003e224bd8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Transform your business idea into a professional online presen
 ce. In this 5-week hands-on series\, you will learn step-by-step how to de
 sign\, build\, and manage your own e-commerce website using WordPress. No 
 coding or prior experience required—perfect for beginners.\nThis is a fi
 ve-day session. Please register only if you are able to attend all\nfive\n
 session\ns\n!\nParticipants will be provided with a pre-configured domain 
 and hosting to use for free during the 5-week course.\nPlease bring your l
 ogo and photos in PNG or JPG format. It’s helpful to have a preferred co
 lor palette and font in mind.\nDate and Time\nSubject\nThursday.      Sept
  24\, 6:00 – 8:00 pm\nGetting Started: WordPress   Fundamentals\nThursda
 y.      Oct\n01\, 6:00 – 8:00 pm\nBranding   & Homepage Design\nThursday
 .      Oct\n08\, 6:00 – 8:00 pm\nNavigation & User Experience\nWednesday
 .  Oct\n14\, 6:00 – 8:00 pm\nE-commerce   & Product Management\nThursday
 .      Oct\n15\,   6:00 – 8:00 pm\nContact Integration & Final   Launch
LOCATION:Scarborough Civic Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8868b44cb69d003e224bd8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f7cb5e6fc10d0550c6c7"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Defending Democracy: Panel Discussion
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T193000
UID:6a96f7cb5e6fc10d0550c6c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What does a healthy democracy look like?\nJoin a panel of expe
 rts to discuss how we can sustain a strong democracy in Toronto. Learn a
 bout key democratic structures and issues\, share ideas\, and discover new
  pathways for civic action. The panel will be followed by a facilitated 
 group discussion focused on thoughtful engagement in today's democratic sy
 stems.\nPanel speakers include:\nDonovan Hayden\nis a community organizer
  at the non-profit Progress Toronto. Along with political organizing\, Do
 novan is a playwright. Through both his political and artistic work he str
 ives to bring people together\, empower them to take action\, and create a
 n impact that tangibly makes their lives better.\nNat Paul\nis the Directo
 r of Education at the Canadian Civil Liberties Association. He oversees r
 ights-focused programming in school and community settings and has present
 ed to a variety of audiences across Canada to\nbuild a sense of ownership 
 and agency with respect to the justice system and the rights and freedoms 
 of people in Canada.\nRania Ahmed\nis the Project Lead at the Democratic E
 ngagement Exchange. She\nhas spent the last seven years bringing people to
 gether around shared goals\, working across health\, education\, sport\, g
 overnment\, and community organizations. She has worked with public secto
 r leaders\, community groups\, and grassroots volunteers alike\, helping p
 eople find common ground and move forward together.\nMelissa Wong\nis the 
 Director of Engagement & Strategic Initiatives at Social Planning Toronto\
 , a community-based organization that challenges inequity in Toronto to ad
 vance positive social and policy change. In her role\, she leads civic and
  community engagement initiatives\, working with a team of Community Plann
 ers to build civic capacity and organize leaders to take action on municip
 al issues. For nine years\, she worked at the municipal level for a Toront
 o City Councillor\, leading campaigns and advancing policy to improve the 
 lives of the city’s most vulnerable residents.\nToronto's municipal elec
 tion takes place on October 26\, 2026. Check out the\nKnowYourVote.TO\nweb
 site and the\nCelebrate Democracy\npage to learn more about the upcoming e
 lection\, access important voter resources\, and discover activities and i
 nteractive library programs for all ages happening at a branch near you.\n
 This initiative is made possible by donations to the Toronto Public Librar
 y Foundation and is generously supported by the McConnell Foundation.\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Malvern\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96f7cb5e6fc10d0550c6c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f3e"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Data Analytics Essentials Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T193000
UID:6a6a661db57350d760b31f3e@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Interested in learning about data analytics? Let's take a free
  online course together in a welcoming space!\nA\nlearning circle\nis a st
 udy group\, guided by library staff\, for people who want to take a free o
 nline course together in a supportive and welcoming environment.\nOrganiza
 tions all over the world recognize the value of analytics. Together\, we'l
 l learn about the essential tools used in this field.\nIn this 12-week lea
 rning circle\, we will work through the Data Analytics Essentials course f
 rom Cisco Networking Academy. We will explore the fundamental tools of a d
 ata analyst\, including how to:\ntransform\, organize and visualize data w
 ith spreadsheet tools like Excel\nquery data from a relational database us
 ing SQL\nimprove data presentations using business intelligence tools like
  Tableau\nWe will meet online every Thursday evening\,\nSeptember 24 - De
 cember 10\, 6-7:30 PM\n(12 sessions).\nParticipants are expected to commit
  to the duration of the course and attend sessions on a weekly basis.\nLea
 rners who complete the course will be able to:\nearn a digital badge\ndown
 load a certificate of completion
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a6a661db57350d760b31f3e
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
