SUMMARY:Reschedule:  Artists in the Library:  Woodland Sunflower Felt Coll
 age
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261001T200000
UID:6a7e5d66b20478002992c363@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Part 1 of a series of workshops for adults\, exploring local f
 lora through embroidery and felt collage.  This event is part of the\nAr
 tists in the Library\nprogram\, hosted by Artist\, Sarah Zanchetta.\nRegis
 tration is required. Space is limited.\nPlease note: Registered participan
 t spaces will be held for 15 minutes after which drop-ins will be allowed.
 \nPlease note: This is a rescheduled program for Wed\, Sept 30\, 2026. The
  new date is Oct 1st\, 2026.\nMeet the Resident:\nSarah Zanchetta (she/the
 y) is a queer textile artist and educator whose practice dives into the lo
 ss of connection and knowledge of poisonous plants in North America. Zanch
 etta uses textiles\, texts\, and hosts community workshops to create intim
 ate works and spaces where we can unfold our curiosities\, care and anxiet
 ies about what grows beside our feet. She holds a Master of Visual Studie
 s from the University of Toronto (2023) and a BFA from OCAD University (20
 18).\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Mount Dennis\, Room 2
