DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 women and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a fragil
 ity fracture in their lifetime. Join a volunteer facilitator from Osteopor
 osis Canada and learn how to improve your bone health\, reduce your risk o
 f osteoporosis and related fractures by exploring the following:\nWhat you
  need to know about bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fracturing a
  bone\nHow to maintain healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical activ
 ity Fall prevention\nPresentations are delivered by trained volunteers on 
 behalf of Osteoporosis Canada.\nRegistration is required. Please register 
 online\, in person or by calling 416-395-5750.\n2-3 PM\nFriday\, October 2
 \, 2026\nFairview Branch\, Room 201\n35 Fairview Mall Drive\, North York\,
  ON M2J 4S4\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
