BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904cc4be148200298a6f8c"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Digital Expo: AI & Democracy
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T163000
UID:6a904cc4be148200298a6f8c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join leading experts for thought-provoking panel discussions e
 xploring the impact of AI on safety\, democracy\, civic participation\, tr
 ust and human flourishing. This registration provides access to all four 
 panel discussions and the exhibitor showcase.\nCan't attend in person? The
  panels will also be livestreamed.\nRegister to receive the viewing link\n
 .\nPanel discussions\nHelping Children Navigate AI Safely\n11:15 am-12 p
 m\nExplore how AI is shaping children's lives and learn practical ways to 
 support safe\, responsible and informed AI use at home and in school.\nFea
 turing Matthew Johnson (MediaSmarts)\, André Côté (The Dais)\, and Aara
 ni Stoneham (AI Literacy Learners)\, with moderation by Jessica Wong (CBC)
 .\nSafeguarding Democracy in the Age of AI\n1-1:45 pm\nJoin this keynote t
 o examine the opportunities and risks AI presents for democracy\, and the 
 steps needed to strengthen trust\, safety and civic participation.\nFeatur
 ing Beatrice Wayne (Samara Centre for Democracy) and Valentine Goddard (AI
  Impact Alliance).\nAI and Civic Engagement\n2-3 pm\nLearn how AI is chang
 ing the way people access information\, engage with one another and partic
 ipate in democracy.\nFeaturing Mathew Markman (Ethelo)\, Jonathan Coutinh
 o (Evidence for Democracy) and Lexa Michaelides (Hypha)\, with moderation
  by Tai Huynh (The Local).\nFlourishing in an AI Society\n3:15-4:15 pm\n
 Discover how communities can help guide AI development toward human flouri
 shing\, trust and democratic values.\nFeaturing Victória Oldemburgo de Me
 llo (Work and Play Lab)\, Jess Mitchell (OCAD University)\, Stephanie Jonn
 son (ODLAN) and Mario Vasilescu (Readocracy)\, with moderation by Pete Bom
 baci (Genwell).\nExhibitor showcase\n9:30 am-4:30 pm\nConnect with educato
 rs and agencies\, and discover the latest tools\, resources\, and solution
 s designed to empower individuals with essential digital skills.\nAI Liter
 acy Learners\nArts Etobicoke\nCompetition Bureau Canada\nConnectTO\nDigita
 l Moment\nMediaSmarts\nOpen Digital Literacy and Access Network (ODLAN)\nP
 op-Up Learning Labs\nReadocracy\nTELUS Wise\n***\nAbout this event\nThis y
 ear's Digital Expo is a dynamic day of learning\, exploration and connect
 ion focused on shaping a responsible AI future for everyone.\nFeaturing in
 spiring speakers and interactive exhibits\, as well as hands-on workshops 
 for adults\, kids\, and teens\, the event explores how emerging technologi
 es are transforming our lives\, communities and civic institutions.\nToget
 her\, we'll examine the opportunities and challenges of AI to foster a mor
 e informed\, inclusive and empowered digital society that protects Canadia
 ns and safeguards democracy.\nSeparate registration is required for each w
 orkshop. Check out\ntpl.ca/digitalexpo\nfor more information about the Exp
 o and the workshops.\n***\nInformation Collection Notice\n: The personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-3975981\, 789 Yon
 ge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.\n***
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Appel Salon\, Second Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a904cc4be148200298a6f8c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
