X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Meetup Toronto Arts And Culture": "https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/315586900/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:meetup_toronto_arts_and_culture
X-SOURCE:Meetup: Toronto Arts & Culture
UID:event_315586900@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260926T045645Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T223000
SUMMARY:Koerner Hall:  Vieux Farka Touré (15% off promo)
DESCRIPTION:TORONTO ARTS & CULTURE\nWe will start off the 26/27 Koerner Ha
 ll concert season\, with a performance by Vieux Farka Touré (from Mali)\,
  and opening for him is Melat Mengesha (from Ethiopia)\n\n(And we have our
  eyes on other concerts during the season!)\n\nAlso we have a 15% off tick
 et promo!! ***Ticket link is below*--($50-$80)**\n\nKnown worldwide for hi
 s electrifying live shows\, Vieux Farka Touré’s virtuosic guitar work b
 lends Malian blues\, rock\, and soul. Winner of Ethiopian Idol Melat Menge
 sha opens the show.\n\nOften referred to as “The Hendrix of the Sahara\,
 ” **Vieux Farka Touré** is the son of legendary Malian guitarist Ali Fa
 rka Touré\, who died in 2006. His live performances are highly energized\
 , and Vieux is known for dazzling crowds with his speed and dexterity on t
 he guitar\, as well as his palpable charisma and luminous smile\, both of 
 which captivate audiences despite any language barriers (though Vieux does
  speak eight languages!).\n\nHailing from Addis Ababa\, Ethiopia\, now bas
 ed in Toronto\, \\*\\*Melat Mengesha’\\*\\*s music features contemporary
 \, folk\, and Ethio-jazz roots sounds. Two major influences in her artisti
 c expression are the legendary Ethiopian singers Gigi (Ejigayehu Shibabaw)
  and Aster Aweke. A major turning point came in 2015\, when Melat won the 
 first season of Balageru (Ethiopian Idol). That breakthrough opened the do
 or to a variety of showcases and performances\, from intimate stages to la
 rge-scale concerts\, allowing her to tour across her hometown and beyond.\
 n\n**TICKET LINK** here:\n\n**PROMO CODE**: ISCULTURE15\n\nhttps://www.rcm
 usic.com/concert/vieux-farka-toure-449801\n\nNote: the PROMO code works fo
 r all pricing--**EXCEPT** the PREMIUM/purple seats
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/toronto-arts-and-culture/events/31558
 6900/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260707T170034Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260707T170034Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Beachmetro": "https://beachmetro.com/event/tanglefoot-reunion/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:beachmetro
X-SOURCE:Beach Metro Community News
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T230000
DTSTAMP:20260910T195312Z
CREATED:20260522T123013Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260910T195312Z
UID:50187-1791057600-1791068400@beachmetro.com
SUMMARY:Tanglefoot Reunion
DESCRIPTION:The Songs\, The Stories\, The Spirit of Canada \nFor three decades\, Tanglefoot carried the spirit of Canada across stages in North America\, the United Kingdom\, and Europe with powerful harmonies\, quick wit\, rich storytelling\, and songs rooted in Canadian history. Now this legendary Canadian folk ensemble returns for a special reunion concert\, bringing their unmistakable energy\, warmth\, and humour back to the stage. \nThis new chapter reunites Canadian Folk Music Award winners Steve Ritchie\, Al Parrish\, Sandra Swannell Young\, and Rob Ritchie\, joined by Rob’s son\, singer and multi-instrumentalist Josh Ritchie\, stepping into the place once held by the late Terry Young. It is both a celebration of legacy and a fresh passing of the torch. \nAudiences can expect fan favourites\, hidden gems\, stories\, laughter\, and the kind of heartfelt music that turns a concert into a shared memory. For longtime fans\, this is a rare chance to reconnect with a beloved part of Canadian folk music. For those discovering Tanglefoot for the first time\, it is an invitation into songs that feel timeless\, spirited\, and deeply Canadian. \nJoin us at Acoustic Harvest for an evening of friendship\, storytelling\, and music that reminds us why live folk music still matters.
URL:https://beachmetro.com/event/tanglefoot-reunion/
LOCATION:Acoustic Harvest\, 200 McIntosh Street\, Scarborough
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://d28bcn7yu97icd.cloudfront.net/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/22083015/event62051.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Acoustic Harvest":MAILTO:acousticharvest@proton.me
END:VEVENT
