SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T200000
UID:6a2d79061e67cd9cb339aa40@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Monday\,\nonce a week for 8 weeks\, August 
 10 - October 5\, 2026\, 5-8 pm\n.\n*Note: Library closed for statutory hol
 iday on September 7\nRegistration closes after week 3\, or when full.\nTTC
  Presto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided fo
 r all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nT
 his program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's WRAP initia
 tive\n. Gerstein Crisis Centre is solely responsible for the protection of
  \npersonal information collected through the program registration \nproce
 ss.
LOCATION:High Park\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a2d79061e67cd9cb339aa40
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95c15536204e08fbb889a8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Postcards of Reconnection: A Craft Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T183000
UID:6a95c15536204e08fbb889a8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Postcards of Reconnection\nSometimes reconnecting starts in so
 litude\, not small talk. In this quiet\, reflective craft workshop\, you
 ’ll design and illustrate a postcard for someone you've been meaning to 
 reach: a friend\, a family member\, or anyone lingering in your thoughts. 
 Take it home\, add a stamp when you're ready and pop it into the mail\, ta
 king the first step towards an important reconnection.\nThis interactive p
 re-show is followed by\nFrom Solitude To Connetion ft. Robert Coplan\,\nwh
 ich starts at 7pm in the North York Central Library Concourse.\nYou can re
 gister for that event\nhere\n\, but please note if you wish to attend the 
 postcard workshop you need to register separately\non this page\n.\n***\nS
 pend an evening rethinking time alone in a room full of other people\n\, a
 s\nwe exp\nlore the\ntheme\nof\n“good solitude” and how alone time mak
 es togetherness possible\n.\nMake the most of your\nConnect IRL\nexperienc
 e by coming before or staying after the\nfeatured event\n. Grab a drink or
  snack at the bar. Sign up for the workshop or try out one of the engageme
 nt activities available\, including the Conversation Station: The Calming 
 Corner\, where you can take a moment or two to connect with a stranger aro
 und the topic of solitude.\nThe\nC\nalming\nCorner\n| 5:30 – 6:30 pm & 8
 :00 – 9:00 pm\nThe Calming Corner offers a calmer\, low-sensory space wi
 th small seating pods of two or three\, prompt cards on solitude and recha
 rge habits\, and no pressure to mingle beyond your comfort zone. It's buil
 t on Coplan's own research that meaningful connection doesn't require cons
 tant stimulation\, just the right amount of space to think before you spea
 k.\nConnect IRL\nis not your average series of events\, workshops and acti
 vities\, but a real chance to connect with other Torontonians in meaningfu
 l and sometimes unexpected ways. Through conversation stations meant to sp
 ark one-on-one conversations\, or hands-on engagement activities and works
 hops before the featured event\, participants can explore the value of con
 nection and community.\n***\nPLAN YOUR VISIT:\nLocation:\nConcourse Event 
 Space\, North York Central Library (5120 Yonge St).\nTime:\nDoors open 5:3
 0pm.\nTickets:\nFree registration required.\nTicket policy:\nWe oversell t
 hese events to ensure that the greatest number of people have an opportuni
 ty to attend. Tickets guaranteed until 5:45pm or until capacity is reached
 . Seating first come\, first served.\nBar\n: Beer/wine available for purch
 ase (debit/credit only).\nAccessibility:\nTPL is committed to accessibilit
 y. If you are Deaf or have a disability and would like to request accommod
 ation for this event\, please contact accessibleservices@tpl.ca or 416-393
 -7099 at least three weeks prior to the event.\n***\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Registrants may be contacted to fill ou
 t a brief survey following the program. Questions about how the library ha
 ndles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@t
 pl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Concourse Event Space\, North York C
 entral Library (5120 Yonge St).
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95c15536204e08fbb889a8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
