SUMMARY:Introduction to Entrepreneurship: Is This for Me\, and Where Do I 
 Start?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261005T200000
UID:6a99b901d94765189bb97c31@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program is part of the Toronto Reference Library's\nEntre
 preneur in Residence\n(EIR) service.\nMost people don't hesitate because t
 heir idea is bad. They hesitate because they think entrepreneurship is int
 imidating. This opening session challenges this assumption by using real C
 anadian statistics and introducing the Business Model Canvas\, both of whi
 ch can help you capture how a business creates value\, reaches customers\,
  and generates capital. By the end of this session\, you will be given a c
 hance to start filling in your own Business Model Canvas and a chance to n
 etwork with other participants.\nThe program includes a short networking c
 omponent\, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with othe
 r entrepreneurs.\nRegistration recommended. Drop-ins welcome until room ca
 pacity is reached.\nTo apply for one-on-one consultations with our residen
 t entrepreneur\, Ryan\, please fill out the in-take form available at\ntpl
 .ca/eir\n. We begin accepting in-take forms on September 28\, 2026 until a
 vailable slots are filled.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal i
 nformation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under t
 he Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informat
 ion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and ev
 aluation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be 
 directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 
 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Beeton Hall\, 1st fl
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
