SUMMARY:1-on-1 Career Consultations with ACCES Employment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T160000
UID:6aa54d81101eb7003f2f7cdf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:1-on-1 Career Consultations with ACCES Employment\nExplore the
  incredible resources and expertise offered by ACCES Employment. Connect w
 ith an Employment Consultant to get tailored resume reviews\, invaluable i
 nterview tips\, and a wealth of additional support.\nBook a\nfree 30-minut
 e appointment\nand embark on a remarkable journey toward your dream job.\n
 Registration is required\n. Limited spots are available. Appointments are 
 limited to one per person.\nREGISTER HERE.\nConsultant #1\nConsultations w
 ill take place in the Business\, Science and Technology Department (\n4th 
 Floor\n). For questions\, email\nclbst@tpl.ca\nor call the North York Cent
 ral Library\, Business\, Science and Technology Department at\n416-395-561
 3\n.\nIf no slots are available on your desired consultation date\, contac
 t ACCES Employment directly for an appointment at\n416-443-9008\n(North Yo
 rk Location) /\n416-921-1800\n(Downtown Location). Or visit\naccesemployme
 nt.ca
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 4th Floor\, Business Science and Tec
 hnology Department
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa54d81101eb7003f2f7cdf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa464b886d8450031156f85"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Google Prompting Essentials: Online Learning Circle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T160000
UID:6aa464b886d8450031156f85@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Ready to develop the skills to use generative AI (GenAI) tools
  effectively and responsibly for work and daily life? Join our staff-facil
 itated Learning Circle to complete the self-paced Google Prompting special
 ization. By completing this Learning Circle program\, you will earn a Goo
 gle Prompting Essentials certificate to share on your resume\, LinkedIn an
 d social media profiles!\nWhat You'll Learn\nThis program is designed for 
 those with some experience with using GenAI. Through short videos\, articl
 es\, assignments and quizzes\, you will discover:\nEssential\nPrompting Sk
 ills\n: How to use a prompting framework to create a desired output with G
 enAI\; how to evaluate and refine your results.\nEveryday Work Tasks:\nStr
 ategies to draft content\, brainstorm ideas\, create tables\, timelines\, 
 and more.\nData & Presentations:\nHow to explore data visualization and us
 e GenAI responsibly when working with data.\nAdvanced Techniques:\nHow to 
 use prompt chaining for complex tasks and prompt versioning to save and re
 use your best prompts over time.\nLearning Circles are study groups guided
  by\nlibrary staff for people who want to complete the Google Prompting sp
 ecialization together in a welcoming space:\nLearners meet weekly and work
  together through course materials.\nParticipants are expected to commit t
 o attending all four Learning Circle sessions.\nSome Experience with GenAI
  Recommended: This course is ideal for participants who have completed the
  AI Essentials course Learning Circle.\nHow to Joi\nn a Learning Circle:\n
 Register once for the first session of this event series\, in order to att
 end all sessions.\nPlease sign up with a valid email address.\nA valid TPL
  library card is required for online circles.\nAttend all four sessions 
 online via Zoom\, on\nTuesdays October 6\, 13\, 20\, 27 from 1:30-4pm.\nR
 egistration is a two-step process. First\, participants must complete thei
 r registration through this page. After this step\, library staff will fol
 low up to request additional information in order to complete the registra
 tion.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa464b886d8450031156f85
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95da92660e510bf440a103"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T150000
UID:6a95da92660e510bf440a103@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google’s free web-based email service.\
 nIn this sixth session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, r
 ead\, reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam a
 nd junk mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basi
 c understanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and ma
 nage your own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisit
 es: Basic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with de
 monstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on 
 this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libr
 aries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only 
 be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Ques
 tions about how the library handles your information can be directed to An
 swerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\,
  Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a95da92660e510bf440a103
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
