UID:6a97324e69166f088b969056@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Digital Inclusion Week: October 4th\, 2026 - October 10th\, 20
 26\nAre you interested in how to navigate the internet on your personal de
 vices with improved privacy\, as well as understanding the importance of s
 taying safe using the internet? If so\, this is the class for you. Learn t
 o develop strong passwords and review the best methods for storing your pa
 sswords.\nCome and join us in this introductory session that is filled wit
 h hands-on activities and discussion.\nPre-requisites: Some computer exper
 ience is required.\nThis program takes place during Digital Inclusion Week
  2026\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning\, sign l
 anguage interpretation\, intervenor services\, or attendant services are a
 vailable upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in adva
 nce to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-events\n.
LOCATION:Bendale\, Program Room
