SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T193000
UID:6aa18f6d101eb7003f2eb029@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learns and predicts outcomes\
 , considerations when using GenAI applications\, and how the Internet of T
 hings (IOT) applies to AI.  All equipment will be provided.  Register 
 via the link provided or call the branch for more information.\nThis progr
 am takes place during Digital Inclusion Week 2026.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Annette Street\, Basement Program Area
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa18f6d101eb7003f2eb029
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults, Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
