X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Civic Tech Toronto": "https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-563-canadian-9q3r8p"}
X-SOURCE-ID:guildhost_civic_tech
SUMMARY:Civic Meetup #563: Canadian Council Records: Nothing but PDFs\, an
 d Toronto
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261006T210000
UID:b73b37703ab1be49521c097862c7f0da@guild.host
DESCRIPTION:Venue not yet confirmed. We're expecting to be at Myhal Centre
  (University of Toronto)\, but please check this page closer to the date f
 or the final location and room number.&#x20\;\n\nTopic: Canadian Council R
 ecords: Nothing but PDFs\, and Toronto\n\nMost Canadian municipalities pub
 lish their council record as PDFs\, sometimes scanned.\n\nA handful of Saa
 S vendors cover roughly 500 cities between them\; the rest are a long tail
  of one-off formats\, and then there's Toronto\, whose minutes are a breat
 h of fresh air.\n\nMike will show what it took to build a searchable recor
 d across both.\n\nSpeaker: Mike Nikles (he/him)\n\nMike is the solo develo
 per behind Civic Lens\, a searchable record of Canadian council meetings\,
  bylaws and municipal spending\, built from the cities' own documents and 
 traced back to source.\n\nAgenda:\n\n7:00-7:20 Welcome and Introductions\n
 \n7:20-7:50 Presentation and Q\\&A/discussion\n\n7:50-9:00 Breakout groups
 \n\n‎\n\nCode of Conduct: https://civictech.ca/about-us\n\n‎\n\nCheck 
 in with us on the Civic Tech Toronto Slack: https://link.civictech.ca/chat
 \n\n‎\n\nAbout Us:\n\nOur weekly civic meetups bring together Torontonia
 ns (designers\, coders\, urban planners\, government staff\, mappers\, pol
 icy-makers\, students\, communications strategists\, community organizers\
 , and more) who share an interest in making Toronto more responsive\, pros
 perous\, sustainable\, and equitable through design\, tech\, and data.\n\n
 Come and be part of it!\n\nFor more info: https://civictech.ca\n\n\\--\n\n
 Interested in speaking at a future event\, or know someone who'd be a grea
 t speaker? We'd love to hear from you:\n\nhttps://link.civictech.ca/speake
 r-suggestions\n\nHave a space that could host up to 80 civic-minded folks 
 for an evening? Consider recommending your venue:\n\nhttps://link.civictec
 h.ca/venue-suggestions\n
LOCATION:Online: https://link.civictech.ca/zoom / Myhal Centre for Enginee
 ring Innovation and Entrepreneurship (MY)
URL:https://guild.host/events/civic-meetup-563-canadian-9q3r8p
X-SOURCE:Civic Tech Toronto
END:VEVENT
