DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T153000
UID:6a8f1597b20478002995add4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Are you ready to separate fact from fiction in a world filled 
 with misinformation and disinformation? Join us for an interactive and ent
 ertaining program where we'll dive into the fascinating world of misinform
 ation\, exploring its origins\, impact\, and how to combat it effectively.
 \nThis program is perfect for curious minds who want to equip themselves w
 ith the skills needed to navigate the complex landscape of online informat
 ion responsibly and safely.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal 
 information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under 
 the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informa
 tion will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and e
 valuation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be
  directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789
  Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Davenport\, Second Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f1597b20478002995add4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
