DESCRIPTION:Join us as we recognize World Mental Health Day (October 10\, 
 2026).\nThis session will explore “Lived Experience” family support pr
 ojects that share the experience and wisdom of families to help other fami
 lies on their own path to recovery and assist educators and health care pr
 actitioners.\nDocumentary Producer\, Stuart Clarfield\, from Mission Media
  Company\, will share video and insight from multiple projects that have m
 obilized the power of ‘Lived Experience’ to help families. His project
 s includes:\nThe Journey Home\n– Documentary DVD\nFinding Our Way\n– B
 ook\nFamily Guide to Mental\nHealth\n– Website\nThis session will includ
 e video clip screenings and discussion followed by Q&A.\nRegistration enco
 uraged but not required.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inf
 ormation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the
  Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The informatio
 n will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and eval
 uation. Questions about how the library handles your information can be di
 rected to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yo
 nge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium (2nd floor)
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aad83743dd190003e72ed13
