X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Torontobotanicalgarden": "https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-designing-with-lilies-tropicals-orchids-3/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:torontobotanicalgarden
X-SOURCE:Toronto Botanical Garden
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261028T210000
DTSTAMP:20260926T005745
CREATED:20260610T182239Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260610T182250Z
UID:10001983-1791396000-1793221200@torontobotanicalgarden.ca
SUMMARY:Floral Design Program: Designing with Lilies\, Tropicals & Orchids
DESCRIPTION:Get ready to unleash your creativity with lilies\, tropicals and orchids in this hands-on floral design class.\nThese are truly special flowers for design\, each having unique characteristics that offer something special for designers. Explore the history of these flowers and key horticultural characteristics\, including their diverse colours\, forms\, and textures. You will also learn how to create outstanding traditional and contemporary arrangements.\n \nCourse fees do not include flowers or supplies. Students are encouraged to find a local flower shop or grocery store to purchase their flowers. A materials list will be e-mailed prior to the start of each class.\n \nPrerequisites: Classic Design Fundamentals I & II.\n \nLearn more about our Certificate in Floral Design\n \nProgram Schedule: Wednesdays\, October 7\, 14\, 21\, & 28\, 6 to 9 p.m.\nPublic $240\, Members $190 (plus applicable taxes and fees)\n \nAbout Pat Ware\nPat has enjoyed teaching a number of different Floral Design courses at the Toronto Botanical Garden. She is a design\, horticultural and rose judge. Pat continues to participate in and learn about Floral Artistry at the local\, provincial and international levels.\n \nAdditional Program Information\n\n\n\nPlease review our Refund Policy and Terms of Agreement.\nFor more information on accessibility at the garden please review our Accessibility Features webpage. If you have any accessibility requirements during your program please email programsupport@torontobotanicalgarden.ca.\nTo learn more about the Toronto Botanical Garden and our programs\, please review our list of Frequently Asked Questions.
URL:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/event/floral-design-program-designing-with-lilies-tropicals-orchids-3/
LOCATION:Toronto Botanical Garden\, 777 Lawrence Ave E\, Toronto\, ON\, M3C 1P2\, Canada
CATEGORIES:Floral Design
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://torontobotanicalgarden.ca/wp-content/uploads/2024/02/0f71a9043dfcd69183089ee05a7ce3d6.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa0693aaafa610029625fc8"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Artist in the Library: Weaving
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T200000
UID:6aa0693aaafa610029625fc8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:October      7:\nThis workshop will teach participants how to 
 build and thread a      hand loom and begin the process of creating woven 
 textiles.\nOctober      14:\nThis workshop will guide participants through
  some beginner      weaving techniques and we’ll begin ideating around o
 ur woven patches for      the community tapestry.\nOctober      21:\nThis 
 workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participants
  to create their patches for the communal tapestry.\nOctober      28:\nThi
 s workshop is a self-led weaving session to make space for      participan
 ts to finish their patches for the communal tapestry. We’ll also      be
  sewing completed patches to the communal tapestry as they are      comple
 ted.\nRegistration required. W\norkshop materials will be provided for the
  first 15 participants. Feel free to drop-in to sessions if you have the s
 upplies needed. We’ll also reflect on and discuss our connections to we
 aving\, water\, and our communities.\nThis event is part of the\nArtists i
