UID:6a909bd42dac6e003722317f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Share the love of reading as members of our book club for kids
  and parents! Read a book together\, then join us once a month at the libr
 ary to chat about the book. Was it a great read? Or a total stinker? All o
 pinions and thoughts are welcome and appreciated. For kids ages 9 to 12 an
 d their grown-ups.\nNo registration required. Copies will be available at 
 the front desk on a first-come\, first-served basis one month before each 
 meeting.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Gallery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a909bd42dac6e003722317f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — School Age
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa9846d65abe8002a796feb"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Dinosaur Fossils and Ancient Life
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T193000
UID:6aa9846d65abe8002a796feb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an interactive presentation about dinosaurs
 \, fossils\, and other ancient natural relics from eons past.  In this pre
 sentation\, you will:\nlearn about the evolutionary origins of various fos
 sil specimens\nlearn about phylogeny and the ‘Tree of Life’\nparticipa
 te in a guided discussion with the presenter and other patrons
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, first floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aa9846d65abe8002a796feb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c967"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Writers Collective of Canada (WCC):  Community Writing Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T200000
UID:6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c967@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Experience the transformative power of writing in an inclusive
  space!\nWriters Collective of Canada (WCC) workshops are unlike any other
 . We write together\, share first drafts in an encouraging environment\, l
 isten deeply to one another\, and receive supportive feedback. Tap into yo
 ur story and explore your voice in an environment of dignity\, courage\, a
 nd respect. (wcc-cec.org)\nNo experience required. Beginners are welcome. 
 Materials are provided.\nWorkshops are not sequential\;\nevery workshop is
  unique. Join ANY session and let’s write together!\nSpace is limited\n.
 \nRegistration required. Call us at 416-393-7683 for more information.
LOCATION:Wychwood\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a58e693cca66c2f00a3c967
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
