SUMMARY:Civic Tech Tools Overview
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261008T200000
UID:6a9c7291be148200298cc795@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A hands-on tour of the tools we will use throughout the progra
 m: from Google Maps and Canva AI to AI research assistants and 3D design s
 oftware. This session is about getting comfortable\, not becoming an exper
 t. By the end you will know what each tool does\, when you would use it\, 
 and how to get started. Think of it as orientation day for the Digital Inn
 ovation Hub.\nThis program is part of TPL's Innovator in Residence series 
 focused on civic innovation. From October 5 to November 28\, join programs
 \, workshops and one-on-one consultations led by technology strategist Ism
 ail Mohamud to learn how technology can help you create positive change in
  your community. Learn more at\ntpl.ca/iir\n.\nInformation Collection Noti
 ce:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Pub
 lic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 
 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program registratio
 n\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your 
 information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 
 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Digital Innovation Hub
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c7291be148200298cc795
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
