SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261009T153000
UID:6a96e0a34cb69d003e24df9c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Downsview branch and its neighbourhood are home to a varie
 ty of trees. Join the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nstaff to explore th
 e natural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize dif
 ferent species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importanc
 e.\nThe tour will start and end at the Downsview branch and will be guide
 d by the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpa
 ved surfaces along the route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for thi
 s outdoor program (e.g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfor
 table shoes). This program takes place rain or shine. In the event of seve
 re inclement weather\, registrants will be notified of an alternative date
 . Children under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThis prog
 ram is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Fr
 iends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Downsview\, ***meeting place?
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a96e0a34cb69d003e24df9c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
