UID:6a8f35bd1b9d9208e0761905@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Led by TIKA\, the seven session workshop series builds towar
 d the creation of individual vision boards.  Workshops will include: visi
 oning creative futures\, dream mapping\, vision board creation and reflect
 ions.  The series is designed to support Black and BIPOC youth.  TIKA is
  a multidisciplinary artist\, composer\, speaker\, and cultural futurist w
 hose work explores healing\, identity\, and collective transformation. Ref
 lective arts-based experiences creates accessible spaces for imagination a
 nd personal growth. Open to all ages 13 plus.\nThis event is part of the\n
 Artists in the Library\nprogram.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pers
 onal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library u
 nder the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The in
 formation will only be used for event and program registration\, delivery 
 and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information c
 an be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\
 , 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Daniel G. Hill\, Quiet Study Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8f35bd1b9d9208e0761905
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
