URL:https://tockify.com/torevent/detail/22868/1792022400000
SUMMARY: Ghost Grain (X Avant XXI: Memory Mannnnn\, Night 1)
DESCRIPTION:Brooklyn based experimental guitarist Ava Mendoza returns to 
 Toronto for a visceral solo performance. Guitarist Andrew Noseworthy & ha
 rpist Grace Scheele bring Christopher Mayo’s compositions to life\, along
  with their own storied improvisations.\n\nAva Mendoza (Natural Ways\, Bi
 ll Orcutt’s Guitar Quartet) creates raw angular guitar pathways with an a
 rray of electronic effects mutating her virtuosic busted blues techniques
  into an all encompassing sonic spectrum. Mendoza’s vocals wind over thes
 e twisted landscapes.\n\nAndrew Noseworthy & Grace Scheele open the night
  with some custom made pieces by composer Christopher Mayo from their lat
 est album “Walk the Darkness Down” https://peopleplacesrecords.bandcamp.c
 om/album/walk-the-darkness-down . Employing rattling tones\, dissonant gu
 itar howls and haunting rhythmic unease the Toronto based duo manifest th
 e perfect score to an October night.\n\nCurated by Tad Michalak\n\nINSTAL
 LATION\nOutside of performances\, attendees can interact with sound sculp
 tures from Night 2 https://musicgallery.org/events/flashback/ artist Step
 hanie Orlando.\n\nInspired by everyday sounds from her time working as a 
 bike mechanic\, Stephanie Orlando’s Sonic Bikes installation invites atte
 ndees to interact with the spectrum of noises and musical textures of rec
 ycled bike parts.\n\nAll prices are inclusive of HST.
CATEGORIES:Concert,First-Unitarian-Church
