SUMMARY:Online Safety
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T153000
UID:6aac254bf9ed2e0038516b6d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In this class we will teach strategies that can be used to ke
 ep personal information\, computers and mobile devices secure when using 
 the Internet.\nThis workshop will cover:\nCreating secure passwords\nUsin
 g public wifi and public computers safely\nProtecting your devices from ma
 lware\nRecognizing identity theft and other scams\nFurther resources\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Deer Park\, Main Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac254bf9ed2e0038516b6d
