BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085db"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Financial Workshops for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085db@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario\, learn m
 ore about government programs\, benefits and eligibility criteria for seni
 ors. These sessions are designed for seniors with low income and those who
  advise them.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Seniors Get?\nLearn about benefits
  for older adults living in Ontario\, including Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\
 , Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS)\, and Guaran
 teed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursday Oct 15: Understanding the
  Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxable income and how can tax cre
 dits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemptions help to reduce taxable inc
 ome.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retirement Income.\nLearn how to re
 duce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if receiving additional income 
 from employment\, a private pension\, or a Registered Retirement Savings P
 lan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada and Leaving Canada.\nLearn 
 about eligible benefits for those that resided in Canada for fewer than 4
 0 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for those planning on emigratin
 g from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26: Tax Credits and Benefits f
 or Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLearn about other tax credits an
 d benefits for seniors\, people with disabilities\, and caregivers\, inclu
 ding the disability tax credit\, the Canada caregiver credit\, and the hom
 e accessibility tax credit.\nRegistration not required. Drop-in welcome.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085db
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
