SUMMARY:In Conversation with Jane Lytvynenko
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261015T200000
UID:6aac2d36a5dbde002aa54c84@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a conversation with Jane Lytvynenko\, one of the l
 eading voices on misinformation\, political manipulation\, and the future 
 of democracy. In an interview-style discussion\, Wency Leung (The Local) w
 ill explore Lytvynenko's research and insights on how misinformation is cr
 eated and spread\, the influence of foreign actors\, and the role social m
 edia plays in shaping public understanding. Together\, they'll discuss wha
 t journalists\, civil society organizations\, and everyday people can do t
 o strengthen a healthy information ecosystem and support democratic resili
 ence.\nFeaturing:\nJane Lytvynenko is a senior technology reporter at NBC 
 News\,  where she covers technology and conflict. Previously\, she covere
 d the war in Ukraine for The Wall Street Journal. She lives in New York.\
 nWency Leung is a senior reporter for\nThe Local\nmagazine\, covering educ
 ation\, health\, and other social issues in the Greater Toronto Area.\nTor
 onto's municipal election takes place on October 26\, 2026. Check out the
 \nKnowYourVote.TO\nwebsite and the\nCelebrate Democracy\npage to learn mor
 e about the upcoming election\, access important voter resources\, and dis
 cover more activities and interactive library programs for all ages happen
 ing at a branch near you.\nThis initiative is made possible by donations t
 o the Toronto Public Library Foundation and is generously supported by the
  McConnell Foundation\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal inform
 ation on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Pu
 blic Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information w
 ill only be used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluat
 ion. Questions about how the library handles your information can be direc
 ted to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge
  Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aac2d36a5dbde002aa54c84
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Preschool
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Teens": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c750e29a7dd0d674955c6"}
