BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Parkdale Pottery": "https://parkdalepottery.ca/products/mold-making-101"}
X-SOURCE-ID:parkdale_pottery
SUMMARY:Mold-Making 101 with Janet Macpherson | 2 Weekends
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261017T160000
UID:parkdale-9903312994587@parkdalepottery.ca
DESCRIPTION:Dates : Saturday and Sunday October 17-18 & 24-25 2026 Times :
  10:00am - 4:00pm Location : 300 Campbell Avenue\, Unit 115 Instructor : J
 anet Macpherson Unlock new creative possibilities in ceramics with our com
 prehensive Mold-Making 101 course. This hands-on class will guide you thro
 ugh the process of designing and creating plaster molds for both slip cast
 ing and press molding techniques. You’ll learn how to craft one-part and
  two-part molds\, make decorative sprig molds\, and combine slip-cast piec
 es into finished ceramic forms. This course is best for those with some ha
 nd-building experience. Throughout the course\, you'll explore: - The fund
 amentals of plaster and its use in mold-making. - Techniques for creating 
 and using press molds and sprig molds. - How to design and construct two-p
 art molds for more complex shapes. - The basics of slip casting and assemb
 ling multi-part pieces. - Finishing techniques to prepare your work for fi
 ring and glazing. What you'll take home: - Your Molds of course! - 1 - 3 S
 lip cast pieces of each mold you complete Please note: 1) Glazing is not p
 art of this course. You can book a glazing session seperately ($50) by ema
 iling the technician at our Dupont Location. Glazing sessions include the 
 use of our studio glazes. Firing fee is included. 2) Due to the hands-on a
 nd cumulative nature of this course\, it's important to attend each sessio
 n as we may not be able to repeat material covered in a missed class in a 
 thorough way although we will try to catch you up. 3) By the end of the co
 urse\, you'll have developed a new set of skills\, a collection of unique 
 molds\, and the confidence to continue exploring mold-making in your own c
 reative practice. ALL WORKSHOPS ARE NON REFUNDABLE
LOCATION:300 Campbell Avenue\, Unit 115\, Toronto\, ON
URL:https://parkdalepottery.ca/products/mold-making-101
X-SOURCE:Parkdale Pottery
END:VEVENT
