SUMMARY:The Garden Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261020T200000
UID:6a84c31960ccaf01c01f27a4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy Gardening? Novice or expert\, join us on the thir
 d Tuesday of the month at 7 pm for an hour of Gardening talks.\nOct 20  
        Planting Bulbs in the Fall for Spring Glory  a Master Garden
 er presentation\nPlanting bulbs in the fall will bring glorious rewards in
  your spring garden. A Toronto Master Gardener will give advice on what to
  plant\, how to plant them and yes\, even a few pointers on squirrels! At 
 the end of the program\, bulbs will be given out to attendees\, while supp
 lies last.\nSuitable for gardeners of any skill level\, with any kind of o
 utdoor space\nNov 17\nAutumn in the Garden  a Master Gardener presentation
 \nDec  15        TBC
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a84c31960ccaf01c01f27a4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
