SUMMARY:NatureTO: Trees Around the Branch Tour
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261022T153000
UID:69aa0118491b809c6f1e6453@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The Maryvale branch and its neighbourhood is home to a variety
  of trees. Join the City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff to explore the na
 tural world on a local neighbourhood tour. Learn how to recognize differen
 t species and fun facts about their cultural and ecological importance.\nC
 hildren under 12 must be accompanied by a parent/caregiver.\nThe tour will
  start and end at the Maryvale branch and will be guided by the City of To
 ronto Urban Forestry staff. There may be uneven\, unpaved surfaces along t
 he route. Please dress and prepare accordingly for this outdoor program (e
 .g. gloves/mittens\, hats\, sunscreen\, water\, comfortable shoes). This p
 rogram takes place rain or shine. In the event of severe inclement weather
 \, registrants will be notified of an alternative date.\nRegistration is r
 equired. Registration is online. For assistance\, please visit the branch 
 or call (416) 396-8931.\nRegistration opens Monday September 21 at 9am.\nI
 nformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is co
 llected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sec
 tions 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for eve
 nt and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how
  the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff 
 at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Maryvale
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69aa0118491b809c6f1e6453
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
