UID:6a8dc7ad4cb69d003e233fb3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on using Google's filters\, tools\, and Maps for absol
 ute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this fifth session you 
 will:\nUse Google search tools more effectively to find websites\, images\
 , and news sites\nExplore Google Maps to find addresses and get directions
  for transit and road travel.\nUpon completion of this class students will
  be able to use more advanced search engine features and use Google Maps a
 t a basic level.\nPrerequisites: Computers for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mo
 use\, keyboarding and internet skills\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstration
 s\nAn introductory class on the Internet for absolute beginners with littl
 e computer experience.\nIn this fourth session you will:\nUnderstand how t
 o read a web site address\nPractice using web addresses\nSearch for inform
 ation using a search engine\nExplore a web site in detail to understand it
 s key components\nUpon completion of this class students will be able to u
 se the internet at a beginner level and complete simple searches.\nPrerequ
 isites: Computer for Beginners 1 & 2 or basic mouse and keyboarding skills
 \nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nTh
 e personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Lib
 rary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). 
 The information will only be used for event and program registration\, del
 ivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informa
