SUMMARY:Family Connections: Workshops for Social & Family Support
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T103000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261109T120000
UID:6ab6a0b6a5dbde002aa72632@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a series of group workshops for anyone navigating 
 relationships\, caregiving responsibilities or family dynamics. Explore th
 e impact these experiences can have on mental health and well-being\, lear
 n practical strategies\, and connect with others in a supportive\, non-jud
 gmental environment. Some workshops are co-facilitated by CMHA Toronto’s
  Family Support Team\, bringing together professional expertise and lived 
 experience to support honest\, practical and compassionate conversations.\
 nRegistration is required. Participants may attend individual workshops or
  complete all eight workshops to receive a certificate.\nTTC Presto ticket
 s will be provided upon request. Snacks and refreshments are provided fo
 r all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program. T
 his program is in collaboration with\nCanadian Mental Health Association T
 oronto.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this 
 form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries
  Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be us
 ed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions
  about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerl
 ine staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toro
 nto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6a0b6a5dbde002aa72632
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
