SUMMARY:A Sufi Storytelling Evening - Conference of the Birds
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261110T143000
UID:6ab2f24aca248a002917abb8@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An inspiring storytelling performance of a Sufi story that is 
 rooted in the literary and folk traditions of West and Central Asia\, and 
 the Middle East. An acclaimed\, world-renowned storyteller tells a story f
 rom “Conference of the Birds\, or “Mantiq – ut – Tayr”\, which i
 s the most beloved epic poem of the 12th century Persian poet and Sufi wri
 ter\, Farid-al-din Attar. The poem tells the story of the struggles of man
  to attain wisdom\, discover absolute truth\, and reach eternal enlightenm
 ent.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Room B
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab2f24aca248a002917abb8
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
