BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:Vibe Coding: Build Your First App with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261111T200000
UID:6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if you could build an app just by describing it\, with no
  coding experience needed? That's vibe coding.\nIn this workshop\, you'll 
 use an AI coding assistant to build your own small\, useful webpage\, chec
 klist\, or organizer from scratch. You'll learn the build loop: describe w
 hat you want\, review the plan\, build one feature\, test it\, fix the bug
 s\, and write documentation so you (or anyone) can understand it later.\nP
 rerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are pro
 vided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will 
 start October 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guarantee
 d after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remainin
 g seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity 
 is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, pl
 ease bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nT
 his program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) o
 n library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this pr
 ogram.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance th
 roughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourag
 e you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending thi
 s program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\
 nGoogle Anti-Gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGo
 ogle AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformat
 ion Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected
  by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 2
 0(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and 
 program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the li
 brary handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nans
 werline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51a71c197d11325d7021
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
