BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T150000
UID:69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:PLEASE NOTE NEW FAIRVIEW LOCATION DUE TO HILLCREST JULY 27 CLO
 SING FOR REPAIRS.\nNew to investing? Learn the basics of this important pa
 rt of financial literacy\, including how to save with\nthe goal of investi
 ng\, types of investments\, how to open an account\, types of accounts\, h
 ow to avoid financial frauds and scams\, and more.\nPresented by the\nCana
 dian Investment Regulatory Organization\n(CIRO) a national self-regulatory
  organization that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers a
 nd trading activity on Canada's debt and equity marketplace.\nRegistration
  is encouraged\n. Drop-ins welcome until capacity is reached.\nInformation
  Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by
  the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a
 )\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and pro
 gram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the libra
 ry handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswer
 line@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fairview\, Program Room 201
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e91f36fca21471b7f0027d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Older Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085dd"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_older_adults
SUMMARY:Financial Workshops for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261112T160000
UID:6a8c4fe960ccaf01c02085dd@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Presented by John Stapleton from Open Policy Ontario\, learn m
 ore about government programs\, benefits and eligibility criteria for seni
 ors. These sessions are designed for seniors with low income and those who
  advise them.\nThursday Oct 1: What Do Seniors Get?\nLearn about benefits
  for older adults living in Ontario\, including Canada Pension Plan (CPP)\
 , Old Age Security (OAS)\, Guaranteed Income Supplement (GIS)\, and Guaran
 teed Annual Income Supplement (GAINS).\nThursday Oct 15: Understanding the
  Personal Income Tax System.\nWhat is a taxable income and how can tax cre
 dits\, deductions\, entitlements and exemptions help to reduce taxable inc
 ome.\nThursday Oct 29: Protecting Your Retirement Income.\nLearn how to re
 duce claw backs to GIS and GAINS payments if receiving additional income 
 from employment\, a private pension\, or a Registered Retirement Savings P
 lan (RRSP).\nThursday Nov 12: Coming to Canada and Leaving Canada.\nLearn 
 about eligible benefits for those that resided in Canada for fewer than 4
 0 years between the ages of 18 and 65\, or for those planning on emigratin
 g from Canada after retiring.\nThursday Nov 26: Tax Credits and Benefits f
 or Seniors and People with Disabilities.\nLearn about other tax credits an
 d benefits for seniors\, people with disabilities\, and caregivers\, inclu
 ding the disability tax credit\, the Canada caregiver credit\, and the hom
 e accessibility tax credit.\nRegistration not required. Drop-in welcome.
LOCATION:Queen/Saulter
