X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6cbfd6074830038298794"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:The Career Confidence & Wellness Series : Overcoming Imposter Synd
 rome
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T170000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T180000
UID:6ab6cbfd6074830038298794@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Have you ever looked at a job posting and thought\, “I could
  never do that”? Or questioned whether you’re actually qualified\, eve
 n when your experience says otherwise? We’ll explore imposter syndrome a
 nd the self-doubt that can show up when applying for jobs\, starting a new
  role\, pursuing opportunities\, or stepping outside your comfort zone. Yo
 u’ll learn how to recognize common patterns of imposter syndrome\, and i
 dentify skills\, strengths\, and accomplishments you may be overlooking. W
 e’ll also explore how self-compassion can help you increase confidence a
 nd trust in yourself.\nThis program is part of TPL's Career Coaches in Res
 idence and is generously supported by our lead donor Azrieli Foundation al
 ong with supporting donors Fidelity Canada\, Friends of Toronto Public Lib
 rary\, South Chapter and\nWilliam and Nona Heaslip Foundation.\nFor more i
 nformation\, please visit\ntpl.ca/careercoach
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab6cbfd6074830038298794
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab418b1607483003829095a"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_adults
SUMMARY:Wellness Recovery Action Plan (WRAP) - Hope + Me
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261119T200000
UID:6ab418b1607483003829095a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:WRAP is for\nanyone\nlooking to strengthen their well-being—
 whether you’re supporting your mental health\, managing stress\, or simp
 ly wanting to feel more balanced and resilient in daily life. Participant
 s will receive a\nWRAP certificate\nupon program completion.\nIn an 8-wee
 k WRAP group\, individuals explore:\nself-care tools like peer connections
 \, relaxation and mindfulness techniques\, stress reduction strategies\, a
 nd more\nresources for keeping well and feeling better in difficult times.
 \nInterested in learning more? Come to a\nvirtual information session\non\
 nOctober 8th at 5-6pm\nThis WRAP Group meets\nevery Thursday\,\nonce a wee
 k for 8 weeks\, October 15 to December 3\n. Registration closes after week
  3\, or when full. Note\, in order to obtain a WRAP certificate at the en
 d of the 8 weeks\, participants need to attend all eight sessions.\nTTC Pr
 esto tickets will be provided.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided for a
 ll participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nThis
  program is in collaboration with Hope + Me. Hope + Me is solely respons
 ible for the protection of personal information collected through the prog
 ram registration process.\nPlease visit the\nHope and Me website to regist
 er
LOCATION:Richview
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6ab418b1607483003829095a
