SUMMARY:Intercultural Communication Competency is a Superpower
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261201T200000
UID:6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:How will having “intercultural communication competence” h
 elp you in your business? As a newcomer\, you have been exposed to differe
 nt customs\, norms\, values\, and communication styles. Entrepreneur in Re
 sidence (Newcomer Focus)\, Jean Chow\, teaches you appropriate and effect
 ive words\, tones\, body gestures and facial expressions when you are nego
 tiating with clients\, vendors\, partners\, employees.\nIn this session:\n
 Adapt your communication in a language that others can understand.\nDispla
 y more respect\, patience\, and sensitivity to others’ feelings and need
 s.\nLearn how managing multicultural teams makes you a more effective lead
 er.\nCome early to network from 6-6:30pm!\nInformation Collection Notice:\
 nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public 
 Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d
 ). The information will only be used for event and program registration\, 
 delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your info
 rmation can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Fort York\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaad774ab7a8e0037c241ff
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
