SUMMARY:Learning Things You Love with AI
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261203T200000
UID:6a9c35d7be148200298cb292@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Always wanted to learn to cook\, draw\, knit\, fix a bike\, or
  speak another language\, but have trouble sticking to it? What if you had
  a personal AI tutor?\nIn this class\, learn how AI can become your person
 al tutor for something you love\, or something new you want to fall in lov
 e with. A tutor explains things in the way you understand\, asks you quest
 ions\, and helps you choose what to learn next. Learn how to turn your goa
 l into a specific\, doable learning experiment: options not answers\, with
  a practice that survives a bad day. Decide ahead of time how you'll know 
 it's working: revise\, or stop without guilt. You'll leave with a plan you
  actually want to try\, and a sense for what AI should never decide for yo
 u.\nPrerequisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers ar
 e provided. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and 
 will start November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be gua
 ranteed after 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, re
 maining seats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until cap
 acity is reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on progra
 m\, please bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Prog
 ram\nThis program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed be
 low) on library laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for t
 his program.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guida
 nce throughout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe en
 courage you to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attendi
 ng this program:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy p
 olicy\nClaude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGo
 ogle Antigravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle
  AI Studio\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation 
 Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by 
 the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)
 \, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and prog
 ram registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the librar
 y handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerl
 ine@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c35d7be148200298cb292
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Teens
END:VEVENT
