SUMMARY:AI for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261210T160000
UID:6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Staying connected with family\, keeping track of appointments\
 , finding programs that interest you. AI can help with everyday things. No
  jargon\, no pressure\, no experience needed.\nIn this class\, you'll lear
 n how AI can help you write a message in your own voice\, turn a spoken th
 ought into a checklist\, plan questions for an appointment\, and find comm
 unity programs. We'll also talk straight about the risks: AI that sounds l
 ike a person deserves caution\, and we'll practice spotting the scams that
  use it. You'll leave with large-print materials\, one personally useful t
 emplate\, and a simple family safety phrase\, all at your own pace.\nPrere
 quisites: Mouse\, keyboarding and internet skills. Computers are provide
 d. No coding experience required.\nRegistration is required and will star
 t November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed a
 fter 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining s
 eats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is 
 reached.\nIf you wish to save your work from this hands-on program\, pleas
 e bring your own USB stick.\nAbout the AI Tools Used in This Program\nThis
  program includes activities that use agentic AI tools (listed below) on l
 ibrary laptops.\nYou do not need to create your own account for this progr
 am.\nParticipants are encouraged to follow the Resident’s guidance throu
 ghout sessions\, which include best practices on using AI.\nWe encourage y
 ou to review the privacy statements of each tool prior to attending this p
 rogram:\nClaude Code\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nCl
 aude Cowork\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle Anti
 gravity\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nGoogle AI Studi
 o\nLearn more about the tool\nReview privacy policy\nInformation Collectio
 n Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toron
 to Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\
 , and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regis
 tration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles
  your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.c
 a\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9c337060ccaf01c0238f67
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
