SUMMARY:Building Your Website with WordPress Session 4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6aaea67bf9ed2e003851e601@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In today's world\, having a personal website is essential for 
 many reasons and especially to support careers and small businesses. Learn
  how to use WordPress to build your own e-commerce or small business websi
 te.\nSession 4: E-COMMERCE\, SECURE PAYMENTS & LAUNCH\nIn this final\, pi
 votal session\, we transform the websites into fully functional online sto
 res. We will cover\nthe comprehensive setup of WooCommerce\, including pro
 duct listing and category management\, with\na major focus on Stripe payme
 nt integration for secure transactions. The session concludes with a final
 \nsite review\, troubleshooting\, and a collaborative Q&A to ensure each p
 articipant feels confident\nmanaging and growing their new online store.\n
 KEYWORDS: WOOCOMMERCE SETUP · PRODUCT LISTING · STRIPE PAYMENT INTEGRATI
 ON · SITE\nREVIEW · Q&A\nLearners who complete all the courses will earn
  a certificate of completion.\n(\nPlease arrive a few minutes early.\nPlea
 se cancel as soon as possible if you are no longer available to attend\n.)
 \nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is
  collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, 
 sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for 
 event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about 
 how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline sta
 ff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W
  2G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6aaea67bf9ed2e003851e601
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Toronto Public Library \u2014 Young Adults": "https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51cb1c197d11325d708b"}
X-SOURCE-ID:tpl_young_adults
SUMMARY:AI At Home: No Cloud\, No Account
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261216T200000
UID:6a9b51cb1c197d11325d708b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:What if your AI didn't need the internet at all: no subscripti
 on\, no one recording what you type?\nIn this class\, you'll see AI models
  running entirely on one computer\, with no connection and no data leaving
  the room. We'll compare a small local model against a powerful cloud mode
 l and plain search: what each gets right\, what each costs\, and what the 
 privacy trade-offs really are. You'll leave with a decision sheet for your
  own hardware\, an installation recipe\, and an honest look at what "open"
  really means when it comes to AI.\nRegistration is required and will star
 t November 9\, 2026 at 12:30 PM.\nNote: Your spot will not be guaranteed a
 fter 5 minutes of the start of the program.\nAfter this time\, remaining s
 eats will be filled on a first come\, first serve basis until capacity is 
 reached.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this
  form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Librarie
 s Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be u
 sed for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Question
 s about how the library handles your information can be directed to Answer
 line staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Tor
 onto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, 2nd Floor eLearning Lab
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a9b51cb1c197d11325d708b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Young Adults
END:VEVENT
